### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Tile set — per tile: label, camp (south/north), centre position, free width/height (area carries free population), enslaved frame thickness (0 for North tiles).
2. Camp headers — title + subtitle text per camp, header positions, title/sub font sizes.
3. Small state — smallFraction (tile scale in SB-A), tinyFraction (fade-in start scale), tile start fill (dark grey) → free fill (teal) colour shift.
4. Centre labels — free label lines ("Free people population" / "(mostly white)"), enslaved label text, label font sizes, arrow paths (two free arrows, one enslaved arrow), arrow colours/widths.
5. Timing — appear start/duration, free-growth start/duration, free-label start/duration, free-label-out start/duration, enslaved start/duration, final hold, total duration.
6. Palette — paper ground, tile grey, tile teal, enslaved rust, ink, label ink, arrow teal, arrow ink, tile-label white.
7. Tile labels — font family, per-tile font rule (scale with tile width, min/max clamps), line wrapping.
8. Easing — per-phase easing names.
9. Phase order — appear < free growth; free label inside the growth window; label-out after growth; enslaved after label-out (validation-enforced).

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent (runtime sampling of config-rendered text): NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; all text is DOM/SVG text rendered from CONFIG strings, the same config-driven principle in its DOM form. Reason stated here per A9.5.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2 (intensity separation · phrase exclusivity): NOT APPLICABLE as particle/sequence cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is construction-level: the two counting rules are different KINDS of mark (area vs frame), never the same mark at two intensities; and the two acts are strictly sequential by the phase-order invariant (Owner Cure 2's exclusivity in schedule form).
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool exists in this technique.
- A9.1 plate construction: NOT APPLICABLE — no moving background plate; the ground is the specimen's still paper ground.
- Family: Packet #12 tile/diagram siblings (T210 grid-map PASS 85.2 · T212 margin bars, attempt in completion) — tile geometry from CONFIG arrays is the family's demonstrated construction; T212's filed lesson (receipt-form discipline, A12/A13) is carried into §5 planning.

## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · headerY 18 · campTitleFontPx 30 · campSubFontPx 17 · centreLabelFontPx 21 · centreSubFontPx 14 · enslavedLabelFontPx 20 · tileLabelScale 0.17 · tileLabelMinPx 20 · tileLabelMaxPx 30 · tinyFraction 0.18 · smallFraction 0.5 · arrowWidthPx 3.5 · freeArrowPaths [[[0.80,0.30],[0.72,0.42],[0.66,0.52]], [[0.80,0.30],[0.84,0.44],[0.90,0.54]]] (normalized stage coords, apex→NC, apex→NY) · enslavedArrowPath [[0.66,0.30],[0.60,0.38],[0.55,0.44]] · tAppearMs 0 · appearDurMs 1500 · headerDurMs 800 · tFreeMs 3000 · freeDurMs 3000 · tFreeLabelMs 3500 · freeLabelDurMs 1500 · tFreeLabelOutMs 10000 · freeLabelOutDurMs 1000 · tEnslavedMs 14500 · enslavedDurMs 2000 · holdMs 4500 · easeAppear/easeFree/easeLabel/easeEnslaved all "easeInOut" · palette {ground #f4f1ea, tileStart #4a4a4a, tile #56706b, enslaved #c85a2e, ink #333333, labelInk #2f2f2f, arrowFree #6fa8a0, arrowDark #2f2f2f, tileLabel #ffffff} · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" · campSouthTitle "South" · campSouthSub "Pro-slavery" · campNorthTitle "North" · campNorthSub "Anti-slavery" · campSouthX 160 · campNorthX 490 · freeLabelLine1 "Free people population" · freeLabelLine2 "(mostly white)" · freeLabelX 320 · freeLabelY 92 · enslavedLabelText "Enslaved people" · enslavedLabelX 415 · enslavedLabelY 92`.
Derived (named, not stored): tile scale at t (phase interpolation tiny→small→free) · tile fill (tileStart→tile lerp by free progress) · frame thickness = enslavedPx × enslavedP · freeLabelOpacity (in by label phase, out by label-out phase) · completeAtMs = tEnslavedMs + enslavedDurMs · durationMs = completeAtMs + holdMs = 21000. **Phase-order invariant (validation-enforced):** tFreeMs ≥ appear end · free-label end ≤ free growth end + freeLabelDurMs (label reveal rides the growth) · tFreeLabelOutMs ≥ free growth end · tEnslavedMs ≥ label-out end — a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped.
Nested: `tiles[12]` — `{label, camp, cx, cy, freeW, freeH, enslavedPx}` (sizes/thicknesses are the §1.3 VISUAL ESTIMATES at the 640 px stage): Virginia south 105,165 150×135 e15 · North Carolina south 232,150 118×118 e11 · South Carolina south 232,245 84×84 e8 · Delaware south 62,262 44×44 e3 · Maryland south 140,282 96×96 e8 · Georgia south 62,330 58×58 e4 · New Jersey south 232,330 84×84 e3 · New York north 432,168 130×130 e0 · Pennsylvania north 558,152 148×138 e0 · Connecticut north 395,262 94×94 e0 · Massachusetts north 558,262 140×128 e0 · New Hampshire north 452,330 76×84 e0. (Count assertion: tiles source-count 12 = built-count 12, harness-printed.)
